CASE 3: MICROSERVICES ARCHITECTURE WITH API GATEWAY AND SERVICE-SPECIFIC LOAD BALANCERS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Suppose ek microservices architecture hai jisme multiple services hain —
jaise User Service, Order Service, Payment Service.

Har service ke multiple instances different servers par run kar rahe hain,
aur har service ka apna Load Balancer hai (jo us service ke instances ke
beech traffic distribute karta hai).

Client ke liye ek Single Entry Point provide karne ke liye API Gateway
rakha jaata hai — jo URL dekh kar request ko appropriate service ke
Load Balancer tak route karta hai.


FLOW:

                                    User
                                      |
                                      | DNS Resolution
                                      v
                              ┌───────────────┐
                              │      DNS      │
                              └───────┬───────┘
                                      |
                                      | returns API Gateway IP
                                      v
                              ┌───────────────┐
                              │  API Gateway  │
                              └───────┬───────┘
                                      |
              ┌───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┐
              |                       |                       |
     /users/**|             /orders/**|           /payments/**|
              v                       v                       v
      ┌──────────────┐        ┌──────────────┐        ┌──────────────┐
      │  User Svc    │        │  Order Svc   │        │ Payment Svc  │
      │  LB          │        │  LB          │        │  LB          │
      └──────┬───────┘        └──────┬───────┘        └──────┬───────┘
             |                       |                       |
       ┌─────┼─────┐           ┌─────┼─────┐           ┌─────┼─────┐
       v     v     v           v     v     v           v     v     v
      ┌───┐ ┌───┐ ┌───┐       ┌───┐ ┌───┐ ┌───┐       ┌───┐ ┌───┐ ┌───┐
      │U-1│ │U-2│ │U-3│       │O-1│ │O-2│ │O-3│       │P-1│ │P-2│ │P-3│
      └───┘ └───┘ └───┘       └───┘ └───┘ └───┘       └───┘ └───┘ └───┘


Yahan:

    - API Gateway    →  Single Entry Point, URL-based routing
    - Service LB     →  Us service ke instances ke beech load balance
    - Service        →  Actual business logic



# NOTE : SINGLE API GATEWAY SPOF BAN SAKTA HAI
-------------------------------------------------

Upar wala architecture small / low-traffic systems ke liye valid hai.
Lekin production me single API Gateway SPOF ban jaata hai — agar wo
down ho gaya, to saari client requests fail ho jaayengi.

Isliye production me multiple API Gateway instances deploy kiye jaate
hain, aur unke aage ek Load Balancer rakha jaata hai.


